# Starting and stopping the project

When asked to start, stop, pause, resume or check the project (or "bring the demo up/down"),
use `scripts/platform_ctl.py` from the repo root. Never improvise with raw API calls first.

```bash
set -a; source .env; set +a                        # credentials; never print them
.venv/bin/python scripts/platform_ctl.py status        # always first: show the user the state
.venv/bin/python scripts/platform_ctl.py stop --dry-run   # show the plan
.venv/bin/python scripts/platform_ctl.py stop          # or: start
.venv/bin/python scripts/platform_ctl.py status        # always last: confirm every layer
```

- Default scope `project` touches only this demo (config/platform.json): CAI app
  "MCC Motor Claim Copilot", model `mcc-approval`, CAI schedules mcc-export-claims, mcc-05, mcc-08
  and mcc-lakehouse-ingest, CDE `rsingh-mcc-*` runs (the live stream included) and the schedules of
  DAGs mcc_motor_claims and mcc_live_stream. Data, Kafka topics and checkpoints are kept, so the
  next stream resumes without gaps.
- `--only cai,cde` limits layers. `--scope platform --yes-shared` also stops or starts the shared
  Kafka Data Hub, CDW `federal-impala-1`, the CDE virtual cluster and the CAI workspace: sibling
  demos use them, so ask the user explicitly before using it, every time.
- CAI schedules are stopped by clearing the cron (API v2 ignores `paused`); start sets the crons
  from `config/platform.json`. Read the state back; do not trust a 200.
- `start` does not run the stream: DAG mcc_live_stream runs it 03:30-13:30 UTC on the scheduled
  dates (config/streaming.json live_window). Ad-hoc demo outside that window:
  `./cde/scripts/mcc_deploy_streaming.sh live 30` (stops itself; never overlaps the 20:30 UTC batch).
- Model endpoint restart takes ~1-3 min, the app ~30 s.
- Afterwards add a short entry to docs/PROJECT_LOG.md and update the README status section.
